From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] filament_scene: accept native frame timing key

The native filament_view plugin sends the frame interval as
`timeSinceLastRenderedSec`, while the example app previously read the
unrelated `deltaTime` key.  Use the native key with a compatibility fallback
and normalize numeric values before invoking update callbacks.

---
 packages/filament_scene/example/lib/events/frame_event_channel.dart | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/filament_scene/example/lib/events/frame_event_channel.dart b/packages/filament_scene/example/lib/events/frame_event_channel.dart
--- a/packages/filament_scene/example/lib/events/frame_event_channel.dart
+++ b/packages/filament_scene/example/lib/events/frame_event_channel.dart
@@ -121,6 +121,10 @@ class FrameEventChannel {
   Future<void> _onPreRenderFrame(JsonObject event) async {
     // Handle preRenderFrame event
-    final deltaTime = event['deltaTime'];
+    final rawDeltaTime =
+        event['timeSinceLastRenderedSec'] ?? event['deltaTime'];
+    final double deltaTime = rawDeltaTime is num
+        ? rawDeltaTime.toDouble()
+        : 0.0;
 
     //
     final scriptTimeStart = DateTime.now().microsecondsSinceEpoch;
